From: lordofthepigs <nicolas.piguet@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:17:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Expose the combat damage assignment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Combat computes, for each damage step, how much of each attacker's damage goes
to each blocker and how much tramples through to the defender. It spends that
table dealing the damage and keeps it private, so afterwards the only trace is
the damage events — which say what landed, not what was chosen. The two differ
whenever prevention or a replacement rewrote the result, and the choice is the
half that trample, deathtouch and banding actually make.

Inert: nothing in Forge calls it. The reader is an external tool that records
what abilities do, and the assignment is the label it needs for a damage step.

The table accumulates over a whole combat and is never cleared, which the
comment says so a reader taking one step at a time knows to difference it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../main/java/forge/game/combat/Combat.java    | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/combat/Combat.java b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/combat/Combat.java
index 79f6139c17f..8438439673d 100644
--- a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/combat/Combat.java
+++ b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/combat/Combat.java
@@ -925,6 +925,24 @@ public class Combat {
         return assignedDamage;
     }
 
+    // ── effect-record instrumentation (price-predictor spec 023) ──────────
+    //
+    // What the assignment settled on, which is the decision trample and
+    // deathtouch actually make: how much of an attacker's damage went to each
+    // blocker and how much through to the defender. It is computed here, spent
+    // on dealing the damage, and afterwards reachable only through the damage
+    // events — which report what landed rather than what was chosen, and the
+    // two differ whenever prevention or a replacement rewrote the result.
+    //
+    // The table accumulates over a whole combat and is never cleared, so a
+    // reader recording one damage step at a time has to difference it against
+    // what it has already seen.
+
+    /** Combat damage as assigned so far this combat, by source and target. */
+    public final Table<Card, GameEntity, Integer> getAssignedDamage() {
+        return damageMap.get();
+    }
+
     public void dealAssignedDamage() {
         final Game game = playerWhoAttacks.getGame();
         game.copyLastState();
